activity-object-state = Object state
activity-object-state-caveat = Classifications are caller reports, not verified facts. Statements, inferences and planning relations grant no authority, run no App or model, and never complete the goal.
activity-object-state-window-caveat = Time windows are reported validity only. Being within a reported window does not make an observation true, current, verified or fresh.
activity-object-state-snapshot-hint = Window status is the broker's projection at the last object-state refresh. Refresh again to update it.
activity-object-state-refresh = Refresh object state
activity-object-state-new = Add observation / relation
activity-object-state-filter = Exact App reference filter (optional)
activity-object-state-filter-hint = Use an exact canonical reference from resources or history, including detached references. Clear this field to list all subjects, then refresh.
activity-object-state-load-hint = Refresh to read shared annotation history. This does not fetch or execute an App.
activity-object-state-empty = No entries were returned for this filter. No object state is inferred.
activity-object-state-limit = At most 100 entries are shown from the shared ledger, which holds at most 1000 per Activity. Filter by reference to narrow history; no local history store is created.
activity-object-state-no-resources = Attach a canonical App object reference to author an observation. Existing history remains readable even without attached resources.
activity-object-state-subject = Subject App reference
activity-object-state-target = Target App reference
activity-object-state-resource-required = Select subject and relation target references already attached to this Activity. The broker validates their canonical form.
activity-object-state-user-statement = User statement (caller classification)
activity-object-state-agent-inference = Agent inference (caller classification)
