activity-object-state-related-to = Related to (planning only)
activity-object-state-depends-on = Depends on (planning only)
activity-object-state-derived-from = Derived from (planning only)
activity-object-state-text = Reported statement / inference (nonempty, at most 4096 UTF-8 bytes)
activity-object-state-note = Relation note (optional, at most 2048 UTF-8 bytes)
activity-object-state-reason = Retraction reason (nonempty, at most 4096 UTF-8 bytes)
activity-object-state-receipt-id = Existing Activity receipt ID
activity-object-state-receipt-required = Enter a valid UUID for an existing Activity receipt.
activity-object-state-app-caveat = An App-linked receipt is still caller_reported, not proof that its result concerns this object. The broker requires an existing same-owner, same-Activity, same-App receipt. No replacement App text is accepted.
activity-object-state-observed-at = Reported window start (RFC3339)
activity-object-state-valid-until = Reported window end (RFC3339)
activity-object-state-window-hint = Leave both fields empty, or supply RFC3339 timestamps with end after start (for example 2026-09-11T12:00:00Z). The broker validates the window. Relations and retractions have no time window.
activity-object-state-unknown = No reported window; validity unknown
activity-object-state-not-yet-applicable = Reported window has not started
activity-object-state-within-window = Within reported window; not verified freshness
activity-object-state-expired = Reported window expired
activity-object-state-entry-id = Entry ID
activity-object-state-draft-id = Submission UUID
activity-object-state-recorded-hint = Broker recording time, not confirmation of observation time or object freshness.
activity-object-state-no-successor = No recorded successor in this response; not a truth or freshness claim.
activity-object-state-superseded = Superseded by { $id }; this historical entry is retained.
activity-object-state-supersedes = Supersedes entry
activity-object-state-detached = This subject reference is detached. History remains readable; reattach the exact canonical reference before appending a correction or retraction.
activity-object-state-correct = Correct with a new entry
activity-object-state-retract = Retract with a reason
activity-object-state-correction-hint = The subject is fixed. This appends a new immutable entry with one predecessor; only one successor is allowed. Stale corrections conflict. Discard and refresh before correcting a newer entry. Retractions cannot be corrected; add a fresh observation instead.
activity-object-state-correction-unavailable = This entry is superseded, retracted, detached or no longer selected. Refresh the history before correcting or retracting it.
activity-object-state-retry-hint = Retrying an unchanged submission reuses this UUID. Editing after a submission creates a new UUID. A timeout may have recorded the entry; retry unchanged before editing to avoid an unintended extra entry.
activity-object-state-save = Record caller report
activity-object-state-discard = Discard draft / refresh history
activity-object-state-recorded = Recorded caller report { $id }. Activity lifecycle is unchanged.

activity-execution-limits = Execution limits
activity-execution-limits-authority-hint = Constraints only: these settings grant no capabilities or approvals. Existing permission gates still apply, and this card never starts an App, model or job or changes the Activity goal state.
activity-execution-limits-reservations-hint = An attempt is durably charged BEFORE its worker starts. A later startup failure or crash can consume it. Retries and recoveries are fresh attempts, not automatic refunds. The turn limit constrains actual model execution.
activity-execution-limits-cancellation-hint = Expiry, disabling, or a policy revision change stops affected running attempts through normal cancellation and lease cleanup. Already-admitted privileged mutations are not promised to be undone.
activity-execution-limits-disable-hint = Turning limits off DISABLES delegated work. It does not remove the configuration or restore unlimited execution.
activity-execution-limits-refresh = Refresh execution limits
activity-execution-limits-configure = Configure execution limits
activity-execution-limits-load-first = Refresh to inspect the broker's execution limits before configuring them. An unloaded card does not mean that no limits exist.
activity-execution-limits-unconfigured = No execution limits are configured. Existing standalone behavior is unchanged; permissions and approvals still apply.
activity-execution-limits-readonly = Configuration and enabling require an active or paused Activity. Inspection and disabling remain available for completed or cancelled Activities.
activity-execution-limits-max-attempts = Maximum lifetime attempts (1-1000)
activity-execution-limits-max-turns = Maximum model turns per attempt (1-100)
activity-execution-limits-expiry = Expiry (RFC3339)
activity-execution-limits-expiry-hint = Enter a future RFC3339 timestamp, for example 2099-01-01T12:00:00Z. The broker checks that expiry is still in the future at transaction time and normalizes it to UTC.
activity-execution-limits-attempts-invalid = Maximum attempts must be a whole number between 1 and 1000.
activity-execution-limits-turns-invalid = Maximum turns per attempt must be a whole number between 1 and 100.
activity-execution-limits-cas-hint = Save uses the revision loaded when this form opened. Stale conflicts remain visible; this form never automatically overwrites a newer configuration. Discard and refresh to inspect newer settings.
activity-execution-limits-no-reset-hint = Changes preserve lifetime usage and the enabled state. Lowering the ceiling below usage is allowed and blocks new attempts; explicitly raising the ceiling may allow more. There is no reset or delete action.
activity-execution-limits-expected-revision = Expected revision for this submission: { $revision }
activity-execution-limits-initial = Initial configuration uses expected_revision: null and is created enabled at revision 1. It does not start work or grant permissions.
activity-execution-limits-save = Save execution limits
activity-execution-limits-discard = Discard draft / refresh limits
activity-execution-limits-enable = Enable delegated work within these limits
activity-execution-limits-disable = Disable delegated work
activity-execution-limits-enabled = Enabled setting; expiry, remaining attempts and permission checks still apply
activity-execution-limits-disabled = Disabled: delegated work is stopped, not restored to unlimited execution
activity-execution-limits-expired = Expired by the displayed local clock; the broker enforces its deadline
activity-execution-limits-not-expired = Expiry not reached by the displayed local clock
activity-execution-limits-exhausted = No attempts remain under this ceiling. Prior charges are retained, including attempts affected by later failures.
activity-execution-limits-attempt-count = Lifetime attempts used: { $used } / Ceiling: { $maximum } / Remaining: { $remaining }
activity-execution-limits-turn-count = Maximum actual model turns per attempt: { $maximum }
activity-execution-limits-revision = Configuration revision: { $revision }
activity-execution-limits-created = Configuration created at
activity-execution-limits-updated = Configuration updated at
activity-execution-limits-snapshot-hint = Settings and counters are from the last limits refresh. Reservations may have advanced; the broker always enforces its current state.
activity-execution-limits-invalid-response = The limits reply did not match the selected Activity, owner, expected revision or requested change, or reduced lifetime usage. No local success was applied; refresh explicitly before trying again.
activity-execution-limits-saved = Execution limits recorded at revision { $revision }. No capabilities or approvals were granted; Activity goal state is unchanged.
activity-execution-limits-enabled-notice = Delegated work enabled within the existing limits at revision { $revision }. Expiry and usage were not reset, and no permissions were granted.
activity-execution-limits-disabled-notice = Delegated work disabled at revision { $revision }. The configuration and lifetime usage remain; unlimited execution is not restored.

activity-monetary-budget = Monetary budget
activity-monetary-budget-accounting-hint = Configured USD accounting uses owner-selected integer micro-USD rates. It is an upper-bound policy, not provider pricing, invoice data, or billing reconciliation.
activity-monetary-budget-reservation-hint = Each model call reserves a conservative configured-accounting upper bound before provider dispatch. Errors, missing usage, retry/fallback ambiguity, or crashes can retain charges or reservations.
activity-monetary-budget-authority-hint = This policy grants no capability or approval, does not replace global AI consent or execution limits, and never changes Activity goal state.
activity-monetary-budget-refresh = Refresh monetary budget
activity-monetary-budget-configure = Configure monetary budget
activity-monetary-budget-load-first = Refresh to inspect the broker's monetary budget. An unloaded card does not mean that no policy exists.
activity-monetary-budget-unconfigured = No monetary budget is configured. Existing model behavior is unchanged.
activity-monetary-budget-readonly = Configuration and enabling require an active or paused Activity. Inspection and disabling remain available for completed or cancelled Activities.
activity-monetary-budget-currency = Fixed currency
activity-monetary-budget-maximum-total = Maximum configured total (micro-USD, 1-1000000000000)
activity-monetary-budget-input-rate = Configured input rate (micro-USD per million tokens)
activity-monetary-budget-output-rate = Configured output rate (micro-USD per million tokens)
activity-monetary-budget-output-limit = Maximum output tokens per turn (1-1000000)
activity-monetary-budget-total-invalid = Maximum configured total must be a whole number between 1 and 1000000000000 micro-USD.
activity-monetary-budget-input-rate-invalid = Configured input rate must be a whole number between 1 and 1000000000000 micro-USD per million tokens.
activity-monetary-budget-output-rate-invalid = Configured output rate must be a whole number between 1 and 1000000000000 micro-USD per million tokens.
activity-monetary-budget-output-limit-invalid = Maximum output tokens per turn must be a whole number between 1 and 1000000.
activity-monetary-budget-cas-hint = Save uses the revision loaded when this form opened. Stale conflicts remain visible and are never automatically rebased. Updates preserve broker-owned spent/reserved accounting and enabled state.
activity-monetary-budget-expected-revision = Expected revision for this submission: { $revision }
activity-monetary-budget-initial = Initial configuration uses expected_revision: null and is created enabled at revision 1. It does not start a model or grant permission.
activity-monetary-budget-save = Save monetary budget
activity-monetary-budget-discard = Discard draft / refresh budget
activity-monetary-budget-enable = Enable model turns within this monetary budget
activity-monetary-budget-disable = Disable monetary-budget model turns
activity-monetary-budget-enabled = Enabled configured-accounting policy
activity-monetary-budget-disabled = Disabled: model turns governed by this policy are blocked, not made unlimited
activity-monetary-budget-total = Configured accounting total: { $value }
activity-monetary-budget-spent = Spent (configured accounting): { $value }
activity-monetary-budget-reserved = Reserved (configured accounting): { $value }
activity-monetary-budget-remaining = Remaining (configured accounting): { $value }
activity-monetary-budget-input-rate-summary = Configured input rate: { $value } micro-USD per 1,000,000 tokens
activity-monetary-budget-output-rate-summary = Configured output rate: { $value } micro-USD per 1,000,000 tokens
activity-monetary-budget-output-limit-summary = Maximum output per turn: { $value } tokens
activity-monetary-budget-revision = Configuration revision: { $revision }
activity-monetary-budget-created = Configuration created at
activity-monetary-budget-updated = Configuration updated at
activity-monetary-budget-snapshot-hint = Values are from the last broker refresh. The ledger may advance; the broker always owns admission, reservation, settlement, and persistence.
activity-monetary-budget-exhausted = No configured accounting balance remains. Actual settlement is never clamped to the configured total.
activity-monetary-budget-invalid-response = The monetary-budget reply did not match the selected Activity, authenticated owner, exact revision, or submitted policy. No local success was applied; refresh before trying again.
activity-monetary-budget-saved = Monetary budget recorded at revision { $revision }. Broker-owned accounting was retained; no permissions were granted.
activity-monetary-budget-enabled-notice = Monetary budget enabled at revision { $revision }. Existing configured accounting and ledger state remain authoritative.
activity-monetary-budget-disabled-notice = Monetary budget disabled at revision { $revision }. The policy and ledger remain; this does not restore unlimited model use.
activity-scheduling-priority = Scheduling priority
activity-scheduling-priority-summary = Current preference: { $priority }. Foreground is preferred over standard and background; standard preserves legacy compatibility; background defers while fresher preferred work is available.
activity-scheduling-priority-semantics = Foreground is preferred at pending admission, standard preserves ordinary compatibility, and background may be deferred while fresher preferred work is available.
activity-scheduling-priority-aging = Admission-only ordering uses deterministic bounded aging: after 30 minutes waiting, aged queued work is admitted before non-aged work in FIFO order.
activity-scheduling-priority-authority = This owner preference grants no authority or capability, bypasses no consent or budget check, proves no completion or execution, and does not preempt or cancel running or approval-waiting work. It is not guaranteed latency or provider QoS.
activity-scheduling-priority-refresh = Refresh scheduling priority
activity-scheduling-priority-configure = Configure scheduling priority
activity-scheduling-priority-load-first = Refresh to inspect the broker's scheduling policy. An unloaded card does not mean that no policy exists.
activity-scheduling-priority-unconfigured = No scheduling priority is configured. Legacy FIFO admission behavior remains unchanged.
activity-scheduling-priority-readonly = Reopen this Activity before changing its scheduling priority.
activity-scheduling-priority-foreground = Foreground
activity-scheduling-priority-standard = Standard
activity-scheduling-priority-background = Background
activity-scheduling-priority-current = Current priority
activity-scheduling-priority-selected = Selected priority
activity-scheduling-priority-cas = This draft keeps its loaded revision. Stale changes are refused and never automatically rebased.
activity-scheduling-priority-cas-hint = Save uses the exact revision loaded when this form opened. Stale conflicts remain visible and are never automatically rebased.
activity-scheduling-priority-expected-revision = Expected revision for this submission: { $revision }
activity-scheduling-priority-initial = Initial configuration uses expected_revision: null. It only records an admission preference and does not start work.
activity-scheduling-priority-save = Save scheduling priority
activity-scheduling-priority-discard = Discard draft / refresh priority
activity-scheduling-priority-revision = Configuration revision: { $revision }
activity-scheduling-priority-created = Configuration created at
activity-scheduling-priority-updated = Configuration updated at
activity-scheduling-priority-invalid-response = The scheduling-priority reply did not match the selected Activity, authenticated owner, exact revision, or submitted priority. No local success was applied; refresh before trying again.
activity-scheduling-priority-saved = Scheduling priority recorded as { $priority } at revision { $revision }. This changes queued admission preference only; no permissions were granted and no running work was preempted.

activity-capability-policy = Capability policy
activity-capability-policy-authority-hint = Constraints only, never permissions or approval grants. Normal uses existing permissions. Missing verbs and empty rules add no constraints and grant nothing.
activity-capability-policy-approval-hint = Ask requires exact, one-shot approval for the primitive, App invocation or session call, even when permission is already held. Decisions remain in the existing approval gate; this card cannot approve anything.
activity-capability-policy-denial-hint = Deny blocks the entire verb and approval escalation. Denying fs.delete alone does not prevent deletion through writes, exec or other allowed operations. This is not a universal sandbox.
activity-capability-policy-revocation-hint = Creating, editing or revoking a policy stops running old-policy attempts through normal cleanup. Already-admitted effects are not undone. This card never starts an App, model or job or changes goal state.
activity-capability-policy-disable-hint = Disabling a configured policy BLOCKS controlled capability use. It does not remove the policy or restore unrestricted behavior.
activity-capability-policy-refresh = Refresh capability policy
activity-capability-policy-configure = Configure capability policy
activity-capability-policy-load-first = Refresh to inspect the broker's policy before configuring it. Unloaded or failed data does not mean that no policy exists.
activity-capability-policy-unconfigured = No capability policy is configured. Existing permissions and approvals still apply; nothing is granted here.
activity-capability-policy-empty = Empty rules add no constraints, not permissions. Any missing verb follows normal authorization while the policy is enabled.
activity-capability-policy-readonly = Creating, editing and enabling require an active or paused Activity. Inspection and disabling remain available in completed or cancelled states.
activity-capability-policy-catalogue-hint = Enter known catalogue verbs. The broker validates compatible scopes; resource-addressing verbs require an explicit same-kind scope rather than raw Wild. Paths must already be canonical and absolute, without placeholders or dot segments. This editor does not copy the catalogue or resolve resources.
activity-capability-policy-cas-hint = Save retains the revision loaded when this form opened. Stale conflicts are displayed, never automatically overwritten or replayed. Discard and refresh to inspect newer policy.
activity-capability-policy-bounds-hint = At most 64 distinct verb rules, 1-32 scopes for Normal/Ask, and 16 KiB for the complete JSON draft. Requests outside the listed scopes are denied.
activity-capability-policy-rule-limit = A capability policy may contain at most 64 distinct verb rules.
activity-capability-policy-scope-limit = Each Normal or Ask rule may contain at most 32 scopes.
activity-capability-policy-verb = Known catalogue verb, for example fs.read
activity-capability-policy-mode-normal = Normal (existing permissions)
activity-capability-policy-mode-ask = Ask (exact one-shot approval)
activity-capability-policy-mode-deny = Deny (whole verb)
activity-capability-policy-deny-whole-verb = This entire verb is denied, with no scopes and no approval escalation.
activity-capability-policy-scope-path = Path
activity-capability-policy-scope-host = Host
activity-capability-policy-scope-name = Name
activity-capability-policy-scope-self = Self-reference
activity-capability-policy-scope-wild = Explicit wildcard
activity-capability-policy-scope-value = Scope value or pattern (inert text)
activity-capability-policy-wild-hint = Explicit wildcard: no additional scope ceiling for this rule. It is not permission.
activity-capability-policy-add-rule = Add rule
activity-capability-policy-remove-rule = Remove rule
activity-capability-policy-add-scope = Add scope
activity-capability-policy-remove-scope = Remove scope
activity-capability-policy-expected-revision = Expected revision for this submission: { $revision }
activity-capability-policy-initial = Initial configuration uses expected_revision: null and starts enabled at revision 1. This grants nothing.
activity-capability-policy-save = Save capability constraints
activity-capability-policy-discard = Discard draft / refresh policy
activity-capability-policy-enable = Enable these capability constraints
activity-capability-policy-disable = Disable controlled capability use
activity-capability-policy-enabled = Policy enabled; ordinary permissions and these constraints both apply
activity-capability-policy-disabled = Policy disabled: controlled capability use is blocked, not unrestricted
activity-capability-policy-revision = Capability policy revision: { $revision }
activity-capability-policy-created = Policy created at
activity-capability-policy-updated = Policy updated at
activity-capability-policy-snapshot-hint = Policy shown at the last explicit refresh. The broker enforces its current policy, not this display snapshot.
activity-capability-policy-invalid-response = The policy reply did not match the Activity, owner, revision or submitted rules. No local success was applied; refresh explicitly before trying again.
activity-capability-policy-saved = Capability constraints recorded at revision { $revision }. No permissions or approvals were granted.
activity-capability-policy-enabled-notice = Capability constraints enabled at revision { $revision }. Existing permissions are still required.
activity-capability-policy-disabled-notice = Capability policy disabled at revision { $revision }. Controlled capability use is blocked; the policy remains stored.
